{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk git diff --no-compact main...HEAD -- docs/ AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..a29bec0\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/AGENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@\n+# Webshop\n+\n+<!-- project-memory:start · managed by docs-init; edit outside these markers -->\n+## Project memory\n+- Start every task at docs/index.md, or at the active spec's tasks.md on a spec\n+  branch, and load only what they link to. Load glossary.md when naming things and\n+  decisions/ before changing a lasting choice.\n+- Answer what the product does from docs/behavior/; open the code only to change it.\n+- Every code change belongs to a spec in docs/specs/. None yet: start one (spec-start).\n+- One branch per spec, named after its slug. The active spec is the one matching the current branch.\n+- Every session adds its line to tasks.md. If something changes mid-way, update spec.md\n+  or plan.md, then recheck every task.\n+- Write specs, plans, tasks, glossary terms and decisions into docs/,\n+  never into SPEC.md, tasks/, CONTEXT.md or docs/superpowers/.\n+- Before opening a pull request, ship the spec (spec-ship); the PR title starts with the slug.\n+<!-- project-memory:end -->\ndiff --git a/CLAUDE.md b/CLAUDE.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..43c994c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/CLAUDE.md\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+@AGENTS.md\ndiff --git a/docs/architecture/boundaries.md b/docs/architecture/boundaries.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..5cd5516\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/architecture/boundaries.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+---\n+area: boundaries\n+---\n+# Boundaries\n+\n+| Module | Path | Domain | May depend on |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Returns | `src/returns.ts` (re-exported by `src/index.ts`); tests in `test/returns.test.ts` | returns | `Order` from `src/orders.ts` through a type-only import; JavaScript built-ins for dates, arithmetic and collections |\ndiff --git a/docs/architecture/contracts.md b/docs/architecture/contracts.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0c38249\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/architecture/contracts.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\n+---\n+area: contracts\n+---\n+# Contracts\n+\n+| Name | Kind | Input | Output | Consumers |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `calculateRefund` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `order: Order`, `items: ReturnItem[]` | Number of cents from `Math.round(subtotal * (1 - order.discountPercent / 100))`, where subtotal sums each entry's quantity times its first matching order line's unit price; throws `Error` for an unmatched product; performs no quantity or delivery validation | `submitReturn`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n+| `submitReturn` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `order: Order`, `items: ReturnItem[]`, optional `now: Date` (defaults to the current time) | New `Return` with copied item entries, the calculated amount and requested status; throws `Error` on validation failure; accepts supplied values without a return-history store | `test/returns.test.ts`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n+| `approveReturn` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `ret: Return` | New top-level `Return` value with approved status; throws `Error` unless the input status is requested | `test/returns.test.ts`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n+| `refundReturn` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `ret: Return` | New top-level `Return` value with refunded status; throws `Error` unless the input status is approved; performs no payment-service call | `test/returns.test.ts`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n+| `RETURN_WINDOW_DAYS` | Exported numeric constant in `src/returns.ts` | Read access | `30`, fixed in source; used with a day length of 86,400,000 milliseconds | `submitReturn`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\ndiff --git a/docs/architecture/data-model.md b/docs/architecture/data-model.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..8004310\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/architecture/data-model.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+---\n+area: data-model\n+---\n+# Data model\n+\n+| Entity | Key fields | Relations |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `Return` | `id` (string, generated as `return-N` using a module-local counter), `orderId`, `items`, `refundCents` (number of cents), `status` (`requested`, `approved` or `refunded`), `requestedAt` (`Date`) | In-memory value defined in `src/returns.ts`; `orderId` references the supplied `Order.id`; embeds `ReturnItem[]` |\n+| `ReturnItem` | `productId` (string), `quantity` (number) | Embedded in `Return.items`; product lookup uses the first matching `Order.lines` entry |\n+| `Order` (returns input) | Returns reads `id`, `lines`, `discountPercent`, `status` and optional `deliveredAt` (`Date`) | Type defined in `src/orders.ts`; supplies `OrderLine[]` to the returns module |\n+| `OrderLine` (returns input) | `productId`, `quantity`, `unitPriceCents` | Embedded in `Order.lines`; provides the recorded price and quantity for a matching `ReturnItem` |\ndiff --git a/docs/architecture/stack.md b/docs/architecture/stack.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..c1bdd14\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/architecture/stack.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@\n+---\n+area: stack\n+---\n+# Stack\n+\n+## Languages and frameworks\n+\n+| Name | Version | Used for |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| TypeScript | Not pinned | Returns functions and types in `src/returns.ts`; shared order types in `src/orders.ts` |\n+| Bun | Not pinned | Running the returns tests with `bun:test` |\n+\n+## Commands\n+\n+| Task | Command |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Test | `bun test` |\ndiff --git a/docs/behavior/returns/calculate-refund.md b/docs/behavior/returns/calculate-refund.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..5dd34ce\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/behavior/returns/calculate-refund.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+---\n+capability: returns/calculate-refund\n+---\n+# Calculate a refund\n+\n+- Customers receive a refund calculation for the submitted quantities using the unit prices recorded on the order. {#value-returned-items}\n+  e.g. An undiscounted order contains two rain jackets at 1990 cents each and one trail map at 850 cents -> returning one jacket produces a refund amount of 1990 cents.\n+\n+- Customers receive a refund calculation reduced by the order's discount percentage. {#apply-order-discount}\n+  e.g. A water bottle has an order price of 2000 cents and the order has a 10 percent discount -> returning the bottle produces a refund amount of 1800 cents.\n+\n+- Customers receive one refund amount rounded to whole cents after the discount is applied to the combined value of the returned entries. {#round-combined-refund}\n+  e.g. Two rain jackets cost 1990 cents each on an order with a 15 percent discount -> returning both produces a refund amount of 3383 cents.\ndiff --git a/docs/behavior/returns/process-return.md b/docs/behavior/returns/process-return.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..a279468\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/behavior/returns/process-return.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+---\n+capability: returns/process-return\n+---\n+# Approve and record a refund\n+\n+- Support can approve a requested return, changing its status to approved. {#approve-requested-return}\n+  e.g. A wool-socks return has status requested -> approving it produces a return with status approved.\n+\n+- Support receives a rejection when approving a return that is already approved or refunded. {#reject-invalid-approval}\n+  e.g. A return already has status approved -> another approval fails with \"A approved return cannot be approved\".\n+\n+- Support can mark an approved return as refunded. {#record-approved-refund}\n+  e.g. A wool-socks return has status approved -> recording its refund produces a return with status refunded.\n+\n+- Support receives a rejection when recording a refund for a return that is requested or already refunded. {#require-approved-refund}\n+  e.g. A return still has status requested -> recording its refund fails with \"Only an approved return can be refunded\".\n+\n+- Support retains the calculated refund amount when approving a return and marking it refunded. {#preserve-refund-amount}\n+  e.g. A requested wool-socks return has a refund amount of 1200 cents -> the approved and refunded results also record 1200 cents.\ndiff --git a/docs/behavior/returns/request-return.md b/docs/behavior/returns/request-return.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..ff3872f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/behavior/returns/request-return.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@\n+---\n+capability: returns/request-return\n+---\n+# Request a return\n+\n+- Customers can request a return only for an order marked delivered with a recorded delivery time. {#require-delivery}\n+  e.g. An order is still paid -> requesting a return fails with \"Only delivered orders can be returned\".\n+\n+- Customers can submit a return exactly 30 days after delivery, but receive a rejection once more than 30 days have elapsed. {#enforce-return-window}\n+  e.g. An order was delivered at 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z -> a return at 2026-01-31T00:00:00Z is accepted, while one a millisecond later is rejected.\n+\n+- Customers must include at least one item in a return request. {#require-items}\n+  e.g. A delivered order is within the return window, but the request has no items -> it fails with \"A return needs at least one item\".\n+\n+- Customers receive a rejection for a return entry whose product is absent from the order. {#require-ordered-product}\n+  e.g. An order contains only wool socks, and the customer requests a headlamp return -> the request fails because the headlamp is not on the order.\n+\n+- Customers must specify a whole-number quantity of at least one for each return entry. {#require-positive-whole-quantity}\n+  e.g. A customer requests a return of 1.5 wool socks -> the request fails with \"Quantity must be a whole number of at least 1\".\n+\n+- Customers receive a rejection when a single return entry exceeds the quantity on the order's first matching line for that product. {#limit-each-entry-quantity}\n+  e.g. An order has one line containing one pair of wool socks, and a return entry requests two -> the request fails with \"Cannot return more wool-socks than were ordered\".\n+\n+- Customers receive a new return in requested status for an accepted submission. {#start-requested}\n+  e.g. An order containing one pair of wool socks was delivered on January 1, 2026, and the customer submits a valid return on January 20 -> the new return has status requested.\ndiff --git a/docs/decisions/2026-10-13-wishlist-module-and-storage.md b/docs/decisions/2026-10-13-wishlist-module-and-storage.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..6b3ddbc\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/decisions/2026-10-13-wishlist-module-and-storage.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+---\n+id: 2026-10-13-wishlist-module-and-storage\n+status: accepted\n+spec: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\n+date: 2026-10-13\n+---\n+# Keep wishlists in an in-memory module\n+\n+## Context\n+\n+The wishlist needs state associated with a caller-supplied customer ID and operations for saving, viewing and removing products.\n+Sanne chose in-memory storage keyed by customer ID and a module-only implementation in this planning session.\n+The approved spec introduces neither sign-in nor a customer entity.\n+\n+## Options\n+\n+- A module-local Map keyed by customer ID: chosen by Sanne to keep storage in memory like the other modules.\n+- Persistent storage: would retain wishlists across restarts but introduce storage infrastructure outside the chosen scope.\n+- Exported TypeScript operations: chosen by Sanne for this repository's integration surface.\n+- A UI: would introduce a presentation surface outside the chosen scope.\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+Implement wishlists in `src/wishlist.ts` with a module-local Map keyed by `customerId`, tests in `test/wishlist.test.ts` and exports from `src/index.ts`.\n+\n+## Consequences\n+\n+The feature can use the existing TypeScript and Bun setup without a database or UI.\n+Wishlists disappear on process restart and are independent in separate processes.\n+The supplied customer ID selects a wishlist; this module does not establish a caller's identity.\n+A future persistence or presentation change needs a new decision and its own spec.\ndiff --git a/docs/glossary.md b/docs/glossary.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..aa72d44\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/glossary.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+- **Customer ID**: A caller-supplied string identifying a customer. Code: `customerId`.\n+- **Refund**: The monetary amount calculated for returned items. Code: `Return.refundCents`.\n+- **Refunded**: The return status labelled as refunded. Code: `ReturnStatus` value `refunded`.\n+- **Return**: A customer's request to send back items from an order. Code: `Return`.\n+- **Return item**: A product and quantity listed in a return. Code: `ReturnItem`.\n+- **Return window**: The period measured from delivery for submitting a return. Code: `RETURN_WINDOW_DAYS`.\n+- **Saved item**: A product a customer has set aside for later consideration.\n+- **Wishlist**: A customer's collection of saved products.\ndiff --git a/docs/index.md b/docs/index.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..33dfdcd\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/index.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@\n+---\n+product: Webshop\n+docs-format: 1\n+---\n+# Webshop\n+\n+## What it is\n+This is a small webshop where customers buy outdoor gear. Customers send items back when they do not fit, and support handles returns and refunds.\n+\n+## Domains\n+| Domain | Covers | Owner |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| returns | Customer returns and refunds | Sanne |\n+| wishlist | Saving, viewing and removing saved products | Sanne |\n+\n+## Behavior\n+See [behavior/](behavior/): one folder per domain, one file per capability, each a short list of claims with IDs.\n+\n+## Architecture\n+See [architecture/](architecture/): one file per area, `stack.md` first.\ndiff --git a/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/plan.md b/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/plan.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..632a9a6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/plan.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@\n+---\n+spec: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\n+---\n+## Approach\n+\n+Implement `src/wishlist.ts` with a module-local Map keyed by `customerId` and a per-customer Map keyed by product ID.\n+Expose synchronous `saveWishlistItem`, `getWishlist` and `removeWishlistItem` operations and their types through `src/index.ts`.\n+Store only product IDs and first-save timestamps; use the existing catalogue lookup to validate saves and resolve current details on reads.\n+Preserve duplicate saves, sort reads newest first and keep every operation within the addressed customer's wishlist.\n+Use `bun:test` claim coverage with explicit dates and distinct customers; retain the [model sketch](reference/data-model.md) and [contract draft](reference/module-design.md) as working material.\n+\n+## Trade-offs\n+\n+Sanne chose process-local storage and exported module operations over persistence or a UI, as recorded in the [accepted decision](../../decisions/2026-10-13-wishlist-module-and-storage.md). This keeps the existing setup and loses wishlist state on restart.\n+\n+## Files\n+\n+```text\n+src/\n+  wishlist.ts      new: store, types and save/view/remove operations\n+  index.ts         changed: re-export wishlist functions and types\n+test/\n+  wishlist.test.ts new: claim coverage and public export verification\n+```\n+\n+## Architecture to update at ship\n+\n+- `docs/architecture/data-model.md`, from [reference/data-model.md](reference/data-model.md).\n+- `docs/architecture/boundaries.md`, from [reference/module-design.md](reference/module-design.md).\n+- `docs/architecture/contracts.md`, from [reference/module-design.md](reference/module-design.md).\n+- `docs/architecture/stack.md`, from [reference/module-design.md](reference/module-design.md).\n+\n+## Risks\n+\n+- A repeated save could replace the original time or move an item; `preserve-first-save` and `newest-first` prove the ordering.\n+- Shared module state could mix customers; `isolate-wishlists` and `isolate-removal` prove separation, with distinct test customers preventing fixture overlap.\n+- Stored product snapshots could return old prices; `current-product-details` proves that reads use the current catalogue.\ndiff --git a/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/reference/data-model.md b/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/reference/data-model.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f22e951\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/reference/data-model.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@\n+Purpose: retain the wishlist data model sketch as working material for implementation and the architecture update at ship.\n+\n+# Wishlist data model sketch\n+\n+This is the proposed model for this spec, not a description of shipped code.\n+\n+| Value | Proposed fields or shape | Relations |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Module-local wishlist store | `Map<string, Map<string, WishlistItem>>` | The outer key is the supplied `customerId`; the inner key is `productId`, allowing one entry per product per customer. |\n+| `WishlistItem` | `productId: string`, `savedAt: Date` | References a catalogue product by ID; stores its first save moment without quantity, name or price snapshots. |\n+| `WishlistProduct` | `productId: string`, `name: string`, `priceCents: number`, `savedAt: Date` | A read projection combining a saved entry with current details from the existing catalogue in `src/products.ts`. |\n+\n+## Storage and reads\n+\n+- Create a customer's inner Map only after a catalogue product has been resolved successfully for the first save.\n+- Copy the supplied save time on insertion. A repeated save returns the existing entry's values without changing its timestamp or position.\n+- Resolve names and prices from the catalogue for each read, then order entries by descending `savedAt`. Equal timestamps retain insertion order.\n+- Return fresh item values and copied dates so callers cannot mutate the stored entries through returned values or the supplied clock value.\n+- Removing an entry addresses only the supplied customer's Map; an empty customer Map can be discarded.\n+- An absent customer Map reads as an empty list. There is no separate customer record or wishlist ID.\n+\n+## Scope of the sketch\n+\n+The spec leaves disappearing catalogue products and stock handling outside this change; this draft adds no behavior for those cases.\n+Catalogue field access must use the existing exports and types when implementation begins; the catalogue itself is outside the change scope.\n+Keep this file as working material after shipping; update `docs/architecture/data-model.md` from the implemented model instead of moving this draft there.\ndiff --git a/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/reference/module-design.md b/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/reference/module-design.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..dab9dfd\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/reference/module-design.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+Purpose: draft the wishlist contracts, module boundary and verification approach that inform implementation and architecture updates at ship.\n+\n+# Wishlist module draft\n+\n+## Public contracts\n+\n+| Export | Proposed contract | Result and errors |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `saveWishlistItem` | `(customerId: string, productId: string, now?: Date): WishlistItem` | Validate catalogue membership and save a product; default `now` to the current time. Return a copy of the new or existing saved entry. Throw `Error` for an unknown product. |\n+| `getWishlist` | `(customerId: string): WishlistProduct[]` | Return the customer's saved products with current names and prices in newest-first order; return an empty list for a customer with no entries. |\n+| `removeWishlistItem` | `(customerId: string, productId: string): void` | Remove the addressed customer's saved entry; throw `Error` if the entry is absent, including when that customer has no wishlist. |\n+| `WishlistItem` | Exported TypeScript type | The stored product ID and first save time described in [the model sketch](data-model.md). |\n+| `WishlistProduct` | Exported TypeScript type | The read projection described in [the model sketch](data-model.md). |\n+\n+Customer IDs are used as supplied; do not add customer lookup, sign-in or normalization.\n+The draft does not promise exact error message text.\n+\n+## Module boundary\n+\n+- Implement the store, types and synchronous operations in `src/wishlist.ts`, using the existing catalogue lookup from `src/products.ts` and JavaScript built-ins.\n+- Re-export the public functions and types through `src/index.ts` using that file's existing export convention.\n+- Put the claim tests in `test/wishlist.test.ts`. The store remains private; tests use distinct customer IDs rather than adding a public reset API.\n+- Use the existing TypeScript and Bun setup. No new packages, configuration, database, UI or changes to the catalogue module are planned.\n+\n+## Verification design\n+\n+- Name behavioral tests with full references such as `wishlist/save-items#save-item`; cover all 12 claims in the approved spec.\n+- Use explicit dates for duplicate-save and ordering examples, without sleeps. Exercise save/read sequences to prove that successful saves actually remain in the customer's wishlist.\n+- For `current-product-details`, arrange for a catalogue price to change between save and read using the existing catalogue test facilities, and restore any changed fixture or mock afterward. Do not add a production catalogue mutation API for this test.\n+- Exercise two customers independently for reads and removal, including a failed removal from a customer without the saved product.\n+- Verify the three functions through `src/index.ts` after adding the barrel exports, and run the complete `bun test` suite for regressions.\n+\n+## Architecture sources at ship\n+\n+- `docs/architecture/boundaries.md`: the Wishlist module, its source and test paths, catalogue dependency and public barrel.\n+- `docs/architecture/contracts.md`: the implemented public contracts listed above.\n+- `docs/architecture/stack.md`: the expanded TypeScript and Bun usage; retain the existing `bun test` command.\n+\n+Keep this draft as working material after shipping; architecture records the verified implementation.\ndiff --git a/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md b/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0839034\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@\n+---\n+id: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\n+kind: feature\n+status: building\n+summary: Customers can save catalogue products to a wishlist and view or remove them.\n+request: Customers can save items to a wishlist.\n+approved: {by: Sanne, via: in session}\n+---\n+# Save items to a wishlist\n+\n+## Why\n+\n+Customers can lose track of products they are interested in but are not ready to buy.\n+Finding those products again takes effort, and customers may never return to complete the purchase.\n+Success means customers return to saved products and those saved products turn into orders.\n+\n+## What changes\n+\n+### Add · wishlist/save-items\n+\n+- Callers can save any catalogue product to a wishlist using a supplied `customerId` string. {#save-item}\n+  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp for customer-1 -> the headlamp is included in customer-1's wishlist.\n+\n+- Callers use one wishlist per `customerId` without signing in or creating a customer record. {#customer-id-wishlist}\n+  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp and then a tent for customer-1 without signing in -> both products belong to the same customer-1 wishlist.\n+\n+- Callers save products without quantities. {#product-only-items}\n+  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp -> the saved item represents the headlamp product without a quantity.\n+\n+- Callers receive an error when saving a product ID that is absent from the catalogue. {#reject-unknown-product}\n+  e.g. A caller tries to save a product ID that the catalogue does not contain -> saving fails with an error.\n+\n+- Callers leave the wishlist unchanged when saving a product already on it, retaining one entry and its original save moment. {#preserve-first-save}\n+  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp at 10:00, a tent at 10:05 and the headlamp again at 10:10 -> the headlamp remains one entry saved at 10:00, behind the tent.\n+\n+### Add · wishlist/view-items\n+\n+- Callers see only the saved products associated with the `customerId` they supply. {#isolate-wishlists}\n+  e.g. Customer-1 has saved a headlamp and customer-2 has saved a tent -> viewing customer-2's wishlist shows only the tent.\n+\n+- Callers see each saved product with its name and the price the catalogue currently holds. {#current-product-details}\n+  e.g. A headlamp was saved when its catalogue price was 3000 cents, and the catalogue now lists it at 3500 cents -> the wishlist shows the headlamp's name and 3500 cents.\n+\n+- Callers see saved products ordered from most recently saved to least recently saved. {#newest-first}\n+  e.g. A headlamp was saved at 10:00 and a tent at 10:05 -> viewing the wishlist returns the tent before the headlamp.\n+\n+- Callers receive an empty list when the supplied `customerId` has no saved products. {#empty-list}\n+  e.g. Customer-1 has no saved products -> viewing customer-1's wishlist returns an empty list without an error.\n+\n+### Add · wishlist/remove-items\n+\n+- Callers can remove a saved product from the wishlist identified by the supplied `customerId`. {#remove-item}\n+  e.g. A caller removes the headlamp saved for customer-1 -> the headlamp no longer appears in customer-1's wishlist.\n+\n+- Callers receive an error when removing a product that is not on the addressed wishlist. {#reject-unsaved-product}\n+  e.g. Customer-1 has saved only a tent, and a caller tries to remove a headlamp from that wishlist -> removal fails with an error.\n+\n+- Callers leave other customers' wishlists unchanged when removing a saved product. {#isolate-removal}\n+  e.g. Customer-1 and customer-2 both saved a headlamp, and a caller removes it for customer-1 -> customer-2's wishlist still contains the headlamp.\n+\n+## Not doing\n+\n+- Sign-in or a new customer entity.\n+- Buying from the wishlist; that belongs to a separate spec.\n+- Sharing wishlists, named lists or multiple lists per customer.\n+- Price or stock alerts.\n+- Quantities or price snapshots on saved items.\n+- Stock handling or behavior for products becoming unavailable or disappearing from the catalogue; the catalogue is currently fixed.\ndiff --git a/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/tasks.md b/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/tasks.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..be3f297\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/tasks.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+---\n+spec: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\n+---\n+Session 2026-10-13: resumed at T1; first message: \"Sanne asked to plan the wishlist with in-memory customer-keyed storage, only a module and tests, a retained data model sketch, and an OK before building.\"\n+Rechecked 2026-10-13 after: Sanne limited Files to code and tests and reserved shipping for an explicit spec-ship request. T1-T4 unchanged; T5 dropped.\n+Session 2026-10-13: resumed at T1; first message: \"continue\".\n+\n+- [x] T1 Add the private customer-keyed store, `WishlistItem` and `saveWishlistItem` in `src/wishlist.ts`; test product-only save results and unknown-product errors in `test/wishlist.test.ts`. -> product-only-items, reject-unknown-product\n+- [x] T2 Add `WishlistProduct` and `getWishlist` in `src/wishlist.ts`; extend `test/wishlist.test.ts` with save/read sequences proving retained saves, one wishlist per customer, duplicate timestamps, isolation, live catalogue details, ordering and empty lists. -> save-item, customer-id-wishlist, preserve-first-save, isolate-wishlists, current-product-details, newest-first, empty-list\n+- [x] T3 Add `removeWishlistItem` in `src/wishlist.ts`; extend `test/wishlist.test.ts` for successful removal, an unsaved-product error and unchanged wishlists for other customers. -> remove-item, reject-unsaved-product, isolate-removal\n+- [x] T4 Re-export the wishlist functions and types from `src/index.ts`, verify the callable exports in `test/wishlist.test.ts`, and run the complete suite. -> check: all three operations work through src/index.ts and bun test passes\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
